# Ex4  2-chlorophenol  TD-DFT, first 5 excited states  --  PBE/def2-TZVP, gas phase
# Geometry: the optimized structure of the same method in Ex1, copied here by ex4_run_one_method.pbs
# as ex4_input_geometry_from_ex1_PBE_gas.xyz.
# RKS instead of UKS: the molecule is closed-shell, so the ground state is identical, and TD-DFT on
# RKS gives pure singlet states. With UKS the 5 roots would mix in triplets (zero oscillator
# strength) and the UV spectrum would lose peaks.
! RKS PBE def2-TZVP def2/J TightSCF

%maxcore 6000

%tddft
  NRoots 5        # first 5 excited states
  TDA    false    # full TD-DFT instead of the Tamm-Dancoff approximation: better oscillator strengths
end

* xyzfile 0 1 ex4_input_geometry_from_ex1_PBE_gas.xyz
